      "id": "claim_4b7af9a4f85f4b32a3939790114a3d51",
      "statement": "The claude-user target prefers the official CLI when `claude --version` succeeds: it runs `claude mcp remove <name> -s user` then `claude mcp add-json <name> <json> -s user` via spawnSync with a fixed binary and argument list (no shell), rejects arguments containing newline/NUL, and treats 'not found' stderr on remove as success; without the CLI it falls back to merging ~/.claude.json.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/console/src/core/mcp/sync.ts",
